tival tents.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>German police probe arson attack on Wuppertal synagogue</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:37134173414646a351c117d28fd037f6de0e3c0c0b7a12e951893c35cdb2a4e9</id><updated>2026-09-19T12:34:25Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T15:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/german-police-probe-arson-attack-on-wuppertal-synagogue/a-79331270--dce70b32746f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/german-police-probe-arson-attack-on-wuppertal-synagogue/a-79331270?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The man detained shortly after allegedly trying to set fire to Wuppertal's synagogue made antisemitic comments to the arresting officers, prosecutors say. The 37-year-old Afghan citizen also had knives in his apartment.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Merz government approves fuel-price discount</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8780b93f6715b27c49d4324611f937d3ff2b629b24b3717cdd1b0f96a00c1606</id><updated>2026-09-19T12:34:25Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T11:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-merz-government-approves-fuel-price-discount/live-79324526--2cf319e4f7c9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-merz-government-approves-fuel-price-discount/live-79324526?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany's coalition government is grappling with record-high fuel prices ahead of two state elections this weekend.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany: Third malaria death linked to Frankfurt Airport</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fe058018ca9af90ce44e70199cd8b04a2b904f84102601772b31d3b9836c04d0</id><updated>2026-09-19T12:34:25Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T16:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-third-malaria-death-linked-to-frankfurt-airport/a-79315012--d744a8a0ae06.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-third-malaria-death-linked-to-frankfurt-airport/a-79315012?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Two new malaria cases have been registered this week near Frankfurt airport, two months after cases first emerged.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Rebels, workers, radicals: The making of 'Red Berlin'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:968de1c73240d93a2fcc411742596a2f3223917cf6b00de7b0d1e5b9334074e3</id><updated>2026-09-19T12:35:25Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T09:14:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/rebels-workers-radicals-the-making-of-red-berlin/a-79325410--afcfe0d2ce3c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/rebels-workers-radicals-the-making-of-red-berlin/a-79325410?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Bloody May, student sit-ins and the squatter movement: Berlin has long been a hotbed for working-class organizing and radical left-wing politics.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Mecklenburg-Western Pomerania: SPD seeks to fend off AfD</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fa8286fe5459956dd1a1c83cb8db45e603b34235274eab26b831c7435d22fb29</id><updated>2026-09-19T12:35:44Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T06:46:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/mecklenburg-western-pomerania-spd-seeks-to-fend-off-afd/a-79330234--336ea67c69c5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/mecklenburg-western-pomerania-spd-seeks-to-fend-off-afd/a-79330234?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">For nearly three decades, the Social Democrats have governed Germany's northeastern state. If they can fend off the AfD, the result may boost the fortunes of the German government's junior coalition partner.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Airport malaria in Germany remains infrequent</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6a15b420a1a0d05d1293820eb3a0f6fd2d09a8ceb2565b8544e63a26247dab60</id><updated>2026-09-19T12:34:25Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T18:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/airport-malaria-in-germany-remains-infrequent/a-79333920--b6e9f1b4961f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/airport-malaria-in-germany-remains-infrequent/a-79333920?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">An outbreak of malaria at Frankfurt Airport this summer has raised alarm. Experts believe parasites probably arrived in a passenger's luggage. But with the onset of fall, the risks of contracting the disease are low.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Saint, sinner or feminist icon: How Mary Magdalene's image evolved through time</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:10475d99568ef46e6b05f329349b3794a26cad58625799bdf37d419860531e14</id><updated>2026-09-19T12:34:25Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T07:06:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/saint-sinner-or-feminist-icon-how-mary-magdalene-s-image-evolved-through-time/a-79293868--1a6f3ade345e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/saint-sinner-or-feminist-icon-how-mary-magdalene-s-image-evolved-through-time/a-79293868?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">From "Apostle of the Apostles" to prostitute, Mary Magdalene has been assigned a wide variety of roles, as a new exhibition shows.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Elversberg: Bundesliga newcomers from tiny town make waves</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9e1008e513888d9b989db3dbc70cc7058483d779cfedd92bb0f166d4c67592fe</id><updated>2026-09-19T12:34:25Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T06:47:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/elversberg-bundesliga-newcomers-from-tiny-town-make-waves/a-77194483--9d72d35ebb6f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/elversberg-bundesliga-newcomers-from-tiny-town-make-waves/a-77194483?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A team from a small southwestern German town of just 7,000 inhabitants made history by sealing promotion to become the 59th club to play in the Bundesliga. Elversberg has got off to a memorable start.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Werner Herzog: Germany's wild man of cinema is back</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c9fdb2404e0224d54167320cc5adda56cdfad936ca6f8aa9bc66f64c0cee64c7</id><updated>2026-09-19T12:34:25Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T16:41:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/werner-herzog-germany-s-wild-man-of-cinema-is-back/a-78949324--4a5372e58812.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/werner-herzog-germany-s-wild-man-of-cinema-is-back/a-78949324?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As his latest movie, "Bucking Fastard," premiered at the Venice Film Festival, DW talked to the boundary-breaking director.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry></feed>
